    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d329">

                <pb facs="0594" n="500" xml:id="pg500"/>

                <head>No. 329.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Sir L. S. Sackville West to Mr.
                        Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 19, 1887</date>.
                        (Received January 21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d329-f1"/> of the 23d of September last, I have the honor inclose to
                    you herewith a copy of a dispatch from the governor-general of Canada to Her
                    Majesty’s secretary of state for the colonies, inclosing a report from his
                    Government on the case of the United States fishing vessel <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Crittenden.</hi></p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L.S. Sackville
                    West.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d329-a1.xml" xpointer="d329-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d329-a2.xml" xpointer="d329-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d329-a3.xml" xpointer="d329-a3"/>
